@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+## Context
+
+The library has no source yet; `src/index.ts` will be the public entry point. TypeScript strict, ESM (NodeNext), no runtime dependencies, tests run with `node --test`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** strict RFC 6901 string-form evaluation; one function now, reusable by later features.
+**Non-Goals:** URI fragment form, pointer mutation/set, returning "not found" without throwing.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Implementation lives directly in `src/index.ts` (no cross-file import, since Node runs the `.ts` tests via type stripping and NodeNext rejects `.ts` specifiers); split it out later if the library grows.
+- Parse by splitting on `/` after checking the leading `/`, then decode each token with a single-pass regex replace of `~0`/`~1` (avoids the `~01` ordering bug), rejecting any remaining `~` not followed by 0/1.
+- Object lookup uses `Object.hasOwn`, so `__proto__`, `toString` etc. do not resolve.
+- Array index must match `/^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$/` and be `< length`; `-` never resolves, per RFC 6901 §4 (it refers to a nonexistent element).
+- Errors are plain `Error` subclass instances with a descriptive message (`JsonPointerError`), distinguishing nothing further.
+- Tests are `test/*.test.ts`, run by `node --test` using Node type stripping.
