+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) is the published standard for this, and several upcoming features will build on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, which returns the value a JSON Pointer string refers to.
+- It throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer, or when it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+- Only the string representation is supported; the URI fragment representation (`#/a/b`) is out of scope.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: parsing and evaluating RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code under `src/` (first source file of the library), with tests.
+- No new dependencies, no breaking changes.
