+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Resolve a pointer against a document
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` SHALL return the value of `document` that the JSON Pointer `pointer` refers to, following RFC 6901 evaluation. The empty string SHALL refer to the whole document. The function SHALL be exported from `src/index.ts`.
+
+#### Scenario: Empty pointer
+- **WHEN** the pointer is `""`
+- **THEN** the whole document is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Object member and array element
+- **WHEN** resolving `/foo/1` against `{"foo": ["a", "b"]}`
+- **THEN** `"b"` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Falsy and null values
+- **WHEN** the pointer refers to `null`, `0`, `false` or `""`
+- **THEN** that value is returned, without error
+
+#### Scenario: Empty member name
+- **WHEN** resolving `/` against `{"": 1}`
+- **THEN** `1` is returned
+
+### Requirement: Escape sequences
+Within a reference token, `~1` SHALL decode to `/` and `~0` SHALL decode to `~`. Any other `~` (not followed by `0` or `1`, or at the end of a token) SHALL make the pointer invalid.
+
+#### Scenario: Escaped characters
+- **WHEN** resolving `/a~1b` and `/m~0n` against `{"a/b": 1, "m~n": 2}`
+- **THEN** `1` and `2` are returned
+
+#### Scenario: Decoding order
+- **WHEN** resolving `/~01` against `{"~1": 7}`
+- **THEN** `7` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Invalid escape
+- **WHEN** the pointer is `/a~2` or `/a~`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Reject invalid pointers
+A non-empty pointer that does not start with `/`, or a pointer that is not a string, SHALL cause an error to be thrown.
+
+#### Scenario: Missing leading slash
+- **WHEN** the pointer is `foo`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: URI fragment form
+- **WHEN** the pointer is `#/foo`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Reject pointers that do not resolve
+An error SHALL be thrown when a reference token does not identify an existing value. Arrays are indexed by tokens that are `0` or a digit sequence without leading zeros; any other token, an index out of range, or the `-` token (the nonexistent element after the last) SHALL NOT resolve. Object members SHALL be matched only as the object's own properties. A token applied to a primitive value (string, number, boolean, null) SHALL NOT resolve.
+
+#### Scenario: Missing member
+- **WHEN** resolving `/missing` against `{"foo": 1}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Inherited property names
+- **WHEN** resolving `/toString`, `/__proto__` or `/constructor` against `{}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Bad array index
+- **WHEN** resolving `/01`, `/-1`, `/1.0`, `/-`, `/2` or `/length` against `["a", "b"]`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Traversing a primitive
+- **WHEN** resolving `/a/b` against `{"a": "text"}` or `{"a": null}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
